drie's local changes to sokol-c3 (https://github.com/floooh/sokol-c3)

Base: sokol-c3 4baf498 (sokol 1c62e3d, indirect draw and dispatch, PR #1651).

To update: copy the new sokol.c3l/ over this folder, then re-apply each item below.

1. c/sokol_warm.h: drie's own file (background shader compiles that fill the driver
   cache). Not in upstream; keep it.
2. c/sokol.c: after `#include "sokol_cmdbuf.h"`, add
       // drie: background shader compiles that fill the driver cache (sokol_warm.h)
       #include "sokol_warm.h"
3. manifest.json: drie's own. Keep it whole (-O2 -DNDEBUG cflags, the mingw, ios,
   ios-sim and linux-aarch64 targets, the linked libraries).
4. c/sokol_gfx.h, GPU timestamps for drie's GpuTimer (gpu_timer.c3, platform/gputimer.c).
   Every hunk is marked "drie patch (GPU timestamps)":
   - declarations of sg_mtl_command_buffer() and sg_mtl_set_pass_timestamps(sample_buffer,
     start_index, end_index), after sg_mtl_command_queue's;
   - in _sg_mtl_backend_t, after `id<MTLCommandBuffer> cmd_buffer;`:
       id<MTLCounterSampleBuffer> ts_buffer; int ts_start, ts_end;
   - _sg_mtl_begin_compute_pass: when ts_buffer is set, the encoder comes from a
     MTLComputePassDescriptor (serial dispatch) with sampleBufferAttachments[0] sampling the
     start and end of the encoder; ts_buffer is cleared;
   - _sg_mtl_begin_render_pass: when ts_buffer is set, pass_desc.sampleBufferAttachments[0]
     samples the vertex stage's start and the fragment stage's end; ts_buffer is cleared;
   - the two functions' implementations, before sg_mtl_command_queue's.
   (The functions are bound in drie's platform/gputimer.c, not in sg.c3.)
5. c/sokol_gfx.h, the pipeline archive (sokol_warm.h): in _sg_mtl_create_pipeline, the render
   pipeline state is made by _sg_warm_render_pipeline(rp_desc, &err, desc->shader.id) (declared
   in place), not by newRenderPipelineStateWithDescriptor. The hunk is marked "drie patch
   (pipeline archive)".
6. c/sokol_gfx.h, _sg_mtl_compile_library: the library is compiled with MTLCompileOptions whose
   preserveInvariance is YES (not options:nil), so that a generated vertex stage's
   [[position, invariant]] gives every pipeline it is in the same depth (a depth prepass's
   and the EQUAL-tested pass after it). The hunk is marked "drie patch (invariant position)".
